Title: molt sweep test fails opaquely in a shallow clone
Created: 2026-10-15
Author: Claude

--- log ---
2026-10-15T17:40Z Claude created

--- body ---
## Context
`tests/test_molt_ticket_sweep.py::test_archive_stages_only_reported[old-erg]`
and `[old-erg-preclosed]` read a historical `tickets/erg` with
`git show 51ee49c:tickets/erg` (`OLD_ERG_REV`, helper `old_erg`). In a
shallow clone that commit is absent, so both cases die with
`CalledProcessError ... exit status 128`, which looks like a regression.

Observed 2026-10-15 in a cloud session (clone depth 50) while reviewing
PR #1437; the same two cases failed on `main`. CI is unaffected
(`.github/workflows/CI.yml` checks out with `fetch-depth: 0`), but cloud
sessions and worktrees made with `--depth` hit it on every full run.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] When `OLD_ERG_REV` is not in the object store, the two cases skip
      with a reason naming the missing commit and the fix (`git fetch --unshallow`)
- [ ] Unchanged behaviour with full history: both cases still run and pass
- [ ] `make check` passes
